Test SEP-2663 Tasks extension lifecycle on the server.

[1mServer Implementation Requirements (SEP-2663):[0m

The server MUST advertise [2mio.modelcontextprotocol/tasks[0m under
[2mcapabilities.extensions[0m and gate the task surface on negotiation.

[1mSync dispatch (no task created):[0m
- A [2mtools/call[0m against a sync-only tool MUST return a flat
  [2mToolResult[0m with [2mresultType:"complete"[0m and a [2mcontent[][0m array.
- It MUST NOT carry [2mtaskId[0m at the top level (that would imply a
  CreateTaskResult).

[1mServer-directed task creation:[0m
- For task-supporting tools, the server decides whether to create a task —
  the client MUST NOT need to opt in via a request param.
- The response MUST be a [2mCreateTaskResult[0m — a flat [2mResult & Task[0m
  intersection: [2mresultType:"task"[0m, plus [2mtaskId[0m / [2mstatus[0m /
  [2mcreatedAt[0m / [2mlastUpdatedAt[0m / [2mttlMs[0m at the top level.
  There MUST NOT be a nested [2mtask[0m wrapper key.

[1mtasks/get DetailedTask:[0m
- Working tasks return [2mstatus[0m and basic metadata; result/error are
  absent.
- Completed tasks MUST inline the original tool result under [2mresult[0m
  with [2mcontent[][0m. There is no separate [2mtasks/result[0m method.

[1mTool errors vs protocol errors (SEP-2663 §error-semantics):[0m
- A tool that ran but reported an error MUST surface as
  [2mstatus:"completed"[0m with [2mresult.isError:true[0m. The status
  [2m"failed"[0m is reserved for protocol-level errors.
- A protocol-level error (server crash, internal failure) MUST surface
  as [2mstatus:"failed"[0m with an inlined [2merror[0m object (JSON-RPC
  error shape: code/message/data) and MUST NOT carry [2mresult[0m.

[1mCancellation:[0m
- [2mtasks/cancel[0m MUST return an empty
  [2m{resultType:"complete"}[0m ack — no task envelope (SEP-2322
  discriminator). The cancelled status is observed via the next
  [2mtasks/get[0m.
- [2mtasks/cancel[0m against a terminal task returns the same empty ack
  (idempotent) — the spec reserves [2m-32602[0m for unknown taskIds only.

[1mRequired server fixtures ([2mtools/list[0m MUST include all):[0m
- [2mgreet[0m — sync-only, returns [2mHello, {name}![0m.
- [2mslow_compute[0m — task-supporting, [2mseconds[0m-second sleep then a
